Stage 6: does the JIT configuration change which SIDE of 1.0 a result lands on?

Taken because the scope changed, not in spite of it. Nobody tries hard at
cross-language performance yet and absolutes are instrumentation -- but R9
names JIT tiering and PGO as a hazard that handicaps a managed INCUMBENT, and
a handicapped incumbent moves a verdict rather than a decimal. This asks the
only question that still matters about the JIT: does any arm cross 1.0, or
change its rough magnitude, when tiering or PGO is turned off?

commit:   38110c1db695d023a56cb521c4c60cc38f760a2c (+ this slice)
payloads: P1.2 (M1 flat), P2.2 (M2, the shape the control plane moves), P3.1 (M3 oneof)
arms:     as stage3. Ratios formed inside each process; the three processes
          differ ONLY in the environment variables named in each header.

The default is tiering ON and PGO ON, which is what a deployed service runs and
is what every other log in this slice used. The other two are the handicap R9
warns about, measured rather than argued.

